.TH WAYINHIBIT 1 "2026-06-29" "wayinhibit 0.6.1" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
wayinhibit \- Wayland idle inhibitor
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY wayinhibit
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.YS
.SY wayinhibit
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.B \-\-
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARG .\|.\|.]
.YS
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wayinhibit
prevents the Wayland compositor from activating the idle state
(screen lock, screen off, suspend) while it is running.
.PP
Without a command,
.B wayinhibit
runs in the foreground and inhibits idle until it receives
.B SIGINT
or
.BR SIGTERM .
.PP
With a command,
.B wayinhibit
runs that command as a child process, inhibits idle for its duration,
and exits with the same exit code.
.PP
Requires a compositor that supports the
.B zwp_idle_inhibit_manager_v1
Wayland protocol.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout " " \fIDURATION\fR
Stop after
.IR DURATION .
Accepted suffixes:
.B s
(seconds),
.B m
(minutes),
.B h
(hours).
Examples:
.BR 30s ,
.BR 5m ,
.BR 2h .
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress all informational output.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pid\-file " " \fIPATH\fR
Write the process ID to
.I PATH
on startup and remove it on exit.
Useful for signaling
.B wayinhibit
from scripts or service managers.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version number and exit.
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Stopped normally: received
.B SIGINT
or
.BR SIGTERM ,
the timeout elapsed (foreground mode), or the child command exited
with status 0 (command mode).
.TP
.B 1
A runtime error occurred (e.g.\& failed to connect to the Wayland compositor).
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments were supplied.
.TP
.I N
In command mode, the exit code of
.I COMMAND
is propagated as\-is.
If
.I COMMAND
was terminated by a signal, the exit code is 128 + signal number.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
Inhibit idle until Ctrl\-C:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
wayinhibit
.EE
.RE
.PP
Inhibit idle for 30 minutes, then stop:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
wayinhibit \-\-timeout 30m
.EE
.RE
.PP
Inhibit idle while a long rsync runs:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
wayinhibit \-\- rsync \-av /src /dst
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run a backup script silently and propagate its exit code:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
wayinhibit \-\-quiet \-\- ./backup.sh
.EE
.RE
.
.SH NOTES
The
.B zwp_idle_inhibit_manager_v1
protocol is supported by most wlroots-based compositors (Sway, Hyprland,
river, labwc) as well as GNOME and KDE on Wayland.
.PP
The process ID is printed on startup (unless
.B \-\-quiet
is set) so that
.B wayinhibit
can be signaled from scripts:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
kill $(wayinhibit | grep -o 'PID: [0-9]*' | grep -o '[0-9]*')
.EE
.RE
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wayland (7),
.BR kill (1),
.BR signal (7)
.
